{"seconds": 45.1, "exit": 0, "final": "Only Ne5! So it's forced: Re6+ Ne5 (forced) Rxe5#. This is mate in 2 moves. This is clearly the best move!\n\n**Best move:** Re6+\n\n**Main line:** Re6+ Ne5 Rxe5#\n\n**Motif:** attraction (or deflection) - the knight is forced to e5 where the rook can deliver checkmate.\n\n**Coaching note (under 80 words):**\n\"When your opponent gives you a check-defending move like Nd3, look for forcing moves that exploit the undefended pieces or the exposed king position. Here, Re6+ is check\u2014White must play Ne5 (only legal move). Then Rxe5 is checkmate: the rook controls the e-file and the king on e2 has no escape squares because its own pawns block it. Always check if a forcing sequence leads to mate before calculating quiet moves.\"\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Re6+\", \"line\": [\"Re6+\", \"Ne5\", \"Rxe5#\"], \"motifs\": [\"attraction\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "8/7p/2pp1r2/2b5/R1P5/2kN3P/4KPPn/3R4 b - - 5 43"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "8/7p/2pp1r2/2b5/R1P5/2kN3P/4KPPn/3R4 b - - 5 43"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "8/7p/2pp1r2/2b5/R1P5/2kN3P/4KPPn/3R4 b - - 5 43"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/7p/2pp1r2/2b5/R1P5/2kN3P/4KPPn/3R4 b - - 5 43", "move": "Rxf2+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/7p/2pp4/2b5/R1P5/2kN3P/4KrPn/3R4 w - - 0 44", "move": "Ke1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/7p/2pp4/2b5/R1P5/2kN3P/5rPn/3RK3 b - - 1 44", "move": "Rf1+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/7p/2pp4/2b5/R1P5/2kN3P/6Pn/3RKr2 w - - 2 45", "move": "Ke2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/7p/2pp4/2b5/R1P5/2kN3P/4K1Pn/3R1r2 b - - 3 45", "move": "Rxd1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/7p/2pp4/2b5/R1P5/2kN3P/4KrPn/3R4 w - - 0 44", "move": "Nxf2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspe